{"id":"mahabharata-5-054","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":54,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 54 · Duryodhana's confidence","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana tells his father not to fear: the Pandavas were helpless in the forest, and now Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Karna and the other mighty warriors stand with him, and he himself is Bhima's equal with the mace. He boasts of his eleven armies and asks Sanjaya what Yudhishthira intends.","kn":"ಹೆದರಬೇಡ ಎಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ತಂದೆಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ: ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಪಾಂಡವರು ಅಸಹಾಯಕರಾಗಿದ್ದರು, ಈಗ ಭೀಷ್ಮ, ದ್ರೋಣ, ಕೃಪ, ಕರ್ಣ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಮಹಾವೀರರು ತನ್ನೊಂದಿಗಿದ್ದಾರೆ, ಗದೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ತಾನೇ ಭೀಮನಿಗೆ ಸಮ. ಹನ್ನೊಂದು ಅಕ್ಷೌಹಿಣಿಗಳ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಬಡಾಯಿ ಕೊಚ್ಚಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನ ಉದ್ದೇಶವೇನೆಂದು ಸಂಜಯನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन पिता से कहता है कि डरें नहीं: वन में पाण्डव असहाय थे, और अब भीष्म, द्रोण, कृप, कर्ण और अन्य महायोद्धा उसके साथ हैं, और वह स्वयं गदा में भीम के बराबर है। वह अपनी ग्यारह अक्षौहिणी सेना की डींग मारकर सञ्जय से पूछता है कि युधिष्ठिर का क्या विचार है।","te":"భయపడవద్దని దుర్యోధనుడు తండ్రికి చెబుతాడు: అడవిలో పాండవులు నిస్సహాయులుగా ఉన్నారు, ఇప్పుడు భీష్ముడు, ద్రోణుడు, కృపుడు, కర్ణుడు మొదలైన మహావీరులు తనతో ఉన్నారు, గదలో తానే భీమునికి సమానుడు. తన పదకొండు అక్షౌహిణుల గురించి గొప్పలు చెప్పి యుధిష్ఠిరుని ఉద్దేశం ఏమిటని సంజయుని అడుగుతాడు.","ta":"அஞ்ச வேண்டாம் என்று துரியோதனன் தந்தையிடம் சொல்கிறான்: காட்டில் பாண்டவர்கள் உதவியற்றிருந்தார்கள், இப்போது பீஷ்மர், த்ரோணர், க்ருபர், கர்ணன் முதலிய வலிய வீரர்கள் தன்னுடன் உள்ளனர், கதைப் போரில் தானே பீமனுக்கு நிகர். தன் பதினோரு அக்ஷௌஹிணிகள் பற்றி வீம்பு பேசி, யுதிஷ்டிரரின் எண்ணம் என்ன என்று ஸஞ்ஜயனிடம் கேட்கிறான்.","ml":"ഭയപ്പെടേണ്ടെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനൻ പിതാവിനോട് പറയുന്നു: കാട്ടിൽ പാണ്ഡവർ നിസ്സഹായരായിരുന്നു; ഇപ്പോൾ ഭീഷ്മർ, ദ്രോണർ, കൃപർ, കർണ്ണൻ തുടങ്ങിയ മഹായോദ്ധാക്കൾ കൂടെയുണ്ട്, ഗദയിൽ താൻ ഭീമന് തുല്യനാണ്. തന്റെ പതിനൊന്നു സേനകളെക്കുറിച്ച് വീമ്പിളക്കി, യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ എന്തു ചെയ്യാനുദ്ദേശിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം സഞ്ജയനോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.54; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"यानसंधिपर्व","titleEn":"Yanasandhi Parva (Debate on peace)","verses":[{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"न भेतव्यं महाराज न शोच्या भवता वयम् ।\nसमर्थाः स्म परान्राजन्विजेतुं समरे विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"You need not be afraid, great king, nor grieve for us; we are able to defeat our enemies in battle, my lord."}},{"n":2,"text":"वनं प्रव्राजितान्पार्थान्यदायान्मधुसूदनः ।\nमहता बलचक्रेण परराष्ट्रावमर्दिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Madhusudana came to the Pandavas in the forest with a great wheel of an army that crushes enemy lands,"}},{"n":3,"text":"केकया धृष्टकेतुश्च धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nराजानश्चान्वयुः पार्थान्बहवोऽन्येऽनुयायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Kekayas, Dhrishtaketu, Dhrishtadyumna son of Prishata, and many other kings followed the Pandavas."}},{"n":4,"text":"इन्द्रप्रस्थस्य चादूरात्समाजग्मुर्महारथाः ।\nव्यगर्हयंश्च संगम्य भवन्तं कुरुभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those great chariot-warriors gathered not far from Indraprastha and, meeting, reproached you together with the Kurus."}},{"n":5,"text":"ते युधिष्ठिरमासीनमजिनैः प्रतिवासितम् ।\nकृष्णप्रधानाः संहत्य पर्युपासन्त भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"They gathered around Yudhishthira, seated clothed in deerskins, with Krishna foremost, and waited on him."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रत्यादानं च राज्यस्य कार्यमूचुर्नराधिपाः ।\nभवतः सानुबन्धस्य समुच्छेदं चिकीर्षवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those lords of men spoke of the need to take the kingdom back, wishing to destroy you with all your kin."}},{"n":7,"text":"श्रुत्वा चैतन्मयोक्तास्तु भीष्मद्रोणकृपास्तदा ।\nज्ञातिक्षयभयाद्राजन्भीतेन भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Bhishma, Drona and Kripa were spoken to by me then, as I was afraid, king, bull of the Bharatas, of the ruin of kin."}},{"n":8,"text":"न ते स्थास्यन्ति समये पाण्डवा इति मे मतिः ।\nसमुच्छेदं हि नः कृत्स्नं वासुदेवश्चिकीर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My belief is that the Pandavas will not keep to the agreement, for Vasudeva wishes to destroy all of us."}},{"n":9,"text":"ऋते च विदुरं सर्वे यूयं वध्या महात्मनः ।\nधृतराष्ट्रश्च धर्मज्ञो न वध्यः कुरुसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Except Vidura, all of you are to be killed by that great one; and Dhritarashtra, knower of dharma, best of the Kurus, is not to be killed."}},{"n":10,"text":"समुच्छेदं च कृत्स्नं नः कृत्वा तात जनार्दनः ।\nएकराज्यं कुरूणां स्म चिकीर्षति युधिष्ठिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having destroyed all of us, dear father, Janardana wishes to make Yudhishthira sole ruler of the Kurus."}},{"n":11,"text":"तत्र किं प्राप्तकालं नः प्रणिपातः पलायनम् ।\nप्राणान्वा संपरित्यज्य प्रतियुध्यामहे परान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What then is timely for us: bowing down, fleeing, or giving up our lives and fighting back?"}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रतियुद्धे तु नियतः स्यादस्माकं पराजयः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्य सर्वे हि पार्थिवा वशवर्तिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In fighting back our defeat is certain, since all the kings are under Yudhishthira's sway."}},{"n":13,"text":"विरक्तराष्ट्राश्च वयं मित्राणि कुपितानि नः ।\nधिक्कृताः पार्थिवैः सर्वैः स्वजनेन च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our lands are disaffected, our friends angry, and we are scorned by all kings and by our own people everywhere."}},{"n":14,"text":"प्रणिपाते तु दोषोऽस्ति बन्धूनां शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nपितरं त्वेव शोचामि प्रज्ञानेत्रं जनेश्वरम् ।\nमत्कृते दुःखमापन्नं क्लेशं प्राप्तमनन्तकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In bowing down there is a fault for our kin for ever. Yet I grieve for my father, the king with wisdom as his eyes, who has fallen into sorrow and endless suffering because of me."}},{"n":15,"text":"कृतं हि तव पुत्रैश्च परेषामवरोधनम् ।\nमत्प्रियार्थं पुरैवैतद्विदितं ते नरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons have blocked the enemies' way, doing it to please me; you know this from long ago, best of men."}},{"n":16,"text":"ते राज्ञो धृतराष्ट्रस्य सामात्यस्य महारथाः ।\nवैरं प्रतिकरिष्यन्ति कुलोच्छेदेन पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those Pandava great chariot-warriors will repay the hatred by destroying the family of King Dhritarashtra with his ministers."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततो द्रोणोऽब्रवीद्भीष्मः कृपो द्रौणिश्च भारत ।\nमत्वा मां महतीं चिन्तामास्थितं व्यथितेन्द्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona, Bhishma, Kripa and Drona's son, seeing me sunk in great worry and with disturbed senses, said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अभिद्रुग्धाः परे चेन्नो न भेतव्यं परंतप ।\nअसमर्थाः परे जेतुमस्मान्युधि जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If our enemies attack us, do not be afraid, scorcher of foes; the enemy cannot defeat us in battle, lord of men."}},{"n":19,"text":"एकैकशः समर्थाः स्मो विजेतुं सर्वपार्थिवान् ।\nआगच्छन्तु विनेष्यामो दर्पमेषां शितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each of us alone is able to defeat all kings. Let them come; we shall take down their pride with sharp arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"पुरैकेन हि भीष्मेण विजिताः सर्वपार्थिवाः ।\nमृते पितर्यभिक्रुद्धो रथेनैकेन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago Bhishma alone defeated all the kings, when his father had died and he was enraged, with one chariot, Bharata."}},{"n":21,"text":"जघान सुबहूंस्तेषां संरब्धः कुरुसत्तमः ।\nततस्ते शरणं जग्मुर्देवव्रतमिमं भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of the Kurus, furious, killed very many of them, and then they sought refuge in this Devavrata out of fear."}},{"n":22,"text":"स भीष्मः सुसमर्थोऽयमस्माभिः सहितो रणे ।\nपरान्विजेतुं तस्मात्ते व्येतु भीर्भरतर्षभ ।\nइत्येषां निश्चयो ह्यासीत्तत्कालममितौजसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Bhishma is highly able to defeat the enemy in battle together with us; so let your fear go, bull of the Bharatas.\" Such was the resolve of those men of boundless might then."}},{"n":23,"text":"पुरा परेषां पृथिवी कृत्स्नासीद्वशवर्तिनी ।\nअस्मान्पुनरमी नाद्य समर्था जेतुमाहवे ।\nछिन्नपक्षाः परे ह्यद्य वीर्यहीनाश्च पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once the whole earth was under the enemy's sway, but today they cannot defeat us in battle; the enemy's wings are clipped, and the Pandavas are weak."}},{"n":24,"text":"अस्मत्संस्था च पृथिवी वर्तते भरतर्षभ ।\nएकार्थाः सुखदुःखेषु मयानीताश्च पार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth stands with us, bull of the Bharatas; the kings I brought share our joys and sorrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"अप्यग्निं प्रविशेयुस्ते समुद्रं वा परंतप ।\nमदर्थे पार्थिवाः सर्वे तद्विद्धि कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"They would enter fire or the sea for my sake, scorcher of foes; know this, best of the Kurus."}},{"n":26,"text":"उन्मत्तमिव चापि त्वां प्रहसन्तीह दुःखितम् ।\nविलपन्तं बहुविधं भीतं परविकत्थने ॥","meaning":{"en":"They laugh at you here as if you were mad, grieving, lamenting in many ways, afraid, when you praise the enemy."}},{"n":27,"text":"एषां ह्येकैकशो राज्ञां समर्थः पाण्डवान्प्रति ।\nआत्मानं मन्यते सर्वो व्येतु ते भयमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each of these kings thinks himself able against the Pandavas; so let the fear that has come to you go."}},{"n":28,"text":"सर्वां समग्रां सेनां मे वासवोऽपि न शक्नुयात् ।\nहन्तुमक्षय्यरूपेयं ब्रह्मणापि स्वयम्भुवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not even Vasava could destroy my whole army, which is imperishable in form, not even Brahma the self-born himself."}},{"n":29,"text":"युधिष्ठिरः पुरं हित्वा पञ्च ग्रामान्स याचति ।\nभीतो हि मामकात्सैन्यात्प्रभावाच्चैव मे प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, leaving his city, begs for five villages; he is afraid of my army and of my power, lord."}},{"n":30,"text":"समर्थं मन्यसे यच्च कुन्तीपुत्रं वृकोदरम् ।\nतन्मिथ्या न हि मे कृत्स्नं प्रभावं वेत्थ भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"You think Kunti's son Vrikodara is capable, but that is false; you do not know my whole power, Bharata."}},{"n":31,"text":"मत्समो हि गदायुद्धे पृथिव्यां नास्ति कश्चन ।\nनासीत्कश्चिदतिक्रान्तो भविता न च कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no one on earth equal to me in mace fighting; none has been, and none will be."}},{"n":32,"text":"युक्तो दुःखोचितश्चाहं विद्यापारगतस्तथा ।\nतस्मान्न भीमान्नान्येभ्यो भयं मे विद्यते क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am trained, used to hardship, and have gone to the end of this knowledge; so I fear neither Bhima nor anyone else anywhere."}},{"n":33,"text":"दुर्योधनसमो नास्ति गदायामिति निश्चयः ।\nसंकर्षणस्य भद्रं ते यत्तदैनमुपावसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is settled that no one equals Duryodhana with the mace; good luck to you, that was when I stayed with Sankarshana."}},{"n":34,"text":"युद्धे संकर्षणसमो बलेनाभ्यधिको भुवि ।\nगदाप्रहारं भीमो मे न जातु विषहेद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"In battle Sankarshana is the only one equal to me, and stronger on earth; Bhima could never withstand a blow of my mace in a fight."}},{"n":35,"text":"एकं प्रहारं यं दद्यां भीमाय रुषितो नृप ।\nस एवैनं नयेद्घोरं क्षिप्रं वैवस्वतक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even one blow I give Bhima in anger, king, would quickly take him to the dreadful house of Vaivasvata."}},{"n":36,"text":"इच्छेयं च गदाहस्तं राजन्द्रष्टुं वृकोदरम् ।\nसुचिरं प्रार्थितो ह्येष मम नित्यं मनोरथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish, king, to see Vrikodara with mace in hand; this has long been my constant wish."}},{"n":37,"text":"गदया निहतो ह्याजौ मम पार्थो वृकोदरः ।\nविशीर्णगात्रः पृथिवीं परासुः प्रपतिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down in battle by my mace, Partha Vrikodara, limbs shattered, lifeless, will fall to the earth."}},{"n":38,"text":"गदाप्रहाराभिहतो हिमवानपि पर्वतः ।\nसकृन्मया विशीर्येत गिरिः शतसहस्रधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even Himalaya, struck by my mace, a mountain, I could shatter at once into a hundred thousand pieces."}},{"n":39,"text":"स चाप्येतद्विजानाति वासुदेवार्जुनौ तथा ।\nदुर्योधनसमो नास्ति गदायामिति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also knows this, and so do Vasudeva and Arjuna: that none equals Duryodhana with the mace."}},{"n":40,"text":"तत्ते वृकोदरमयं भयं व्येतु महाहवे ।\nव्यपनेष्याम्यहं ह्येनं मा राजन्विमना भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So let your fear of Vrikodara in the great battle go; I will remove him; do not be dejected, king."}},{"n":41,"text":"तस्मिन्मया हते क्षिप्रमर्जुनं बहवो रथाः ।\nतुल्यरूपा विशिष्टाश्च क्षेप्स्यन्ति भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he is killed by me, many chariot-warriors, equal and better, will quickly throw Arjuna down, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":42,"text":"भीष्मो द्रोणः कृपो द्रौणिः कर्णो भूरिश्रवास्तथा ।\nप्राग्ज्योतिषाधिपः शल्यः सिन्धुराजो जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Drona's son, Karna, Bhurishravas, the lord of Pragjyotisha, Shalya, the Sindhu king Jayadratha:"}},{"n":43,"text":"एकैक एषां शक्तस्तु हन्तुं भारत पाण्डवान् ।\nसमस्तास्तु क्षणेनैतान्नेष्यन्ति यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"each of these is able to kill the Pandavas, Bharata; together they will send them in a moment to Yama's house."}},{"n":44,"text":"समग्रा पार्थिवी सेना पार्थमेकं धनंजयम् ।\nकस्मादशक्ता निर्जेतुमिति हेतुर्न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see no reason why the whole earth's army could not defeat Partha Dhananjaya alone."}},{"n":45,"text":"शरव्रातैस्तु भीष्मेण शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nद्रोणद्रौणिकृपैश्चैव गन्ता पार्थो यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha will go to Yama's house by hundreds and thousands of arrows from Bhishma, Drona, Drona's son and Kripa."}},{"n":46,"text":"पितामहो हि गाङ्गेयः शंतनोरधि भारत ।\nब्रह्मर्षिसदृशो जज्ञे देवैरपि दुरुत्सहः ।\nपित्रा ह्युक्तः प्रसन्नेन नाकामस्त्वं मरिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The grandfather Gangeya, Shantanu's son, was born like a Brahmin sage, hard for even the gods to endure; his father, pleased, told him: \"You will not die unless you wish.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"ब्रह्मर्षेश्च भरद्वाजाद्द्रोण्यां द्रोणो व्यजायत ।\nद्रोणाज्जज्ञे महाराज द्रौणिश्च परमास्त्रवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona was born of the Brahmin sage Bharadvaja in a pot; from Drona was born Drona's son Ashvatthama, supreme in weapons."}},{"n":48,"text":"कृपश्चाचार्यमुख्योऽयं महर्षेर्गौतमादपि ।\nशरस्तम्बोद्भवः श्रीमानवध्य इति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa, chief of teachers, glorious, born in a clump of reeds from the great sage Gautama, I think cannot be killed."}},{"n":49,"text":"अयोनिजं त्रयं ह्येतत्पिता माता च मातुलः ।\nअश्वत्थाम्नो महाराज स च शूरः स्थितो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"These three are of unnatural birth: father, mother and uncle of Ashvatthama; and that hero stands with me."}},{"n":50,"text":"सर्व एते महाराज देवकल्पा महारथाः ।\nशक्रस्यापि व्यथां कुर्युः संयुगे भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these great chariot-warriors, great king, are like gods and could trouble even Indra in battle."}},{"n":51,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणकृपाणां च तुल्यः कर्णो मतो मम ।\nअनुज्ञातश्च रामेण मत्समोऽसीति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think Karna equal to Bhishma, Drona and Kripa; Rama himself said, \"You are like me.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"कुण्डले रुचिरे चास्तां कर्णस्य सहजे शुभे ।\nते शच्यर्थे महेन्द्रेण याचितः स परंतपः ।\nअमोघया महाराज शक्त्या परमभीमया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna had a pair of beautiful, natural earrings, which scorcher of foes was asked for by Mahendra for Shachi's sake, and in return he got an unfailing, most fearsome spear."}},{"n":53,"text":"तस्य शक्त्योपगूढस्य कस्माज्जीवेद्धनंजयः ।\nविजयो मे ध्रुवं राजन्फलं पाणाविवाहितम् ।\nअभिव्यक्तः परेषां च कृत्स्नो भुवि पराजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could Dhananjaya live, embraced by that spear? My victory is certain, king, as a fruit placed in the hand; and the defeat of the enemy on earth is plain."}},{"n":54,"text":"अह्ना ह्येकेन भीष्मोऽयमयुतं हन्ति भारत ।\nतत्समाश्च महेष्वासा द्रोणद्रौणिकृपा अपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Bhishma kills ten thousand in a single day, Bharata, and Drona, Drona's son and Kripa, great archers, are the same."}},{"n":55,"text":"संशप्तानि च वृन्दानि क्षत्रियाणां परंतप ।\nअर्जुनं वयमस्मान्वा धनंजय इति स्म ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are also sworn bands of kshatriyas who have said, \"We shall kill Arjuna, or Dhananjaya will kill us.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"तांश्चालमिति मन्यन्ते सव्यसाचिवधे विभो ।\nपार्थिवाः स भवान्राजन्नकस्माद्व्यथते कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those kings think themselves enough for slaying Savyasachin; so why do you grieve so suddenly, king?"}},{"n":57,"text":"भीमसेने च निहते कोऽन्यो युध्येत भारत ।\nपरेषां तन्ममाचक्ष्व यदि वेत्थ परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"And with Bhimasena slain, who else of them could fight, Bharata? Tell me, if you know, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":58,"text":"पञ्च ते भ्रातरः सर्वे धृष्टद्युम्नोऽथ सात्यकिः ।\nपरेषां सप्त ये राजन्योधाः परमकं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the enemy, the five brothers, Dhrishtadyumna and Satyaki are the seven warriors, their greatest strength."}},{"n":59,"text":"अस्माकं तु विशिष्टा ये भीष्मद्रोणकृपादयः ।\nद्रौणिर्वैकर्तनः कर्णः सोमदत्तोऽथ बाह्लिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But ours are the superior ones: Bhishma, Drona, Kripa and the rest, Drona's son, Karna Vaikartana, Somadatta, Bahlika,"}},{"n":60,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषाधिपः शल्य आवन्त्योऽथ जयद्रथः ।\nदुःशासनो दुर्मुखश्च दुःसहश्च विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"the lord of Pragjyotisha, Shalya, the Avanti kings, Jayadratha, Duhshasana, Durmukha and Duhsaha, lord of men,"}},{"n":61,"text":"श्रुतायुश्चित्रसेनश्च पुरुमित्रो विविंशतिः ।\nशलो भूरिश्रवाश्चोभौ विकर्णश्च तवात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutayus, Chitrasena, Purumitra, Vivimshati, Shala, Bhurishravas, and your son Vikarna."}},{"n":62,"text":"अक्षौहिण्यो हि मे राजन्दशैका च समाहृताः ।\nन्यूनाः परेषां सप्तैव कस्मान्मे स्यात्पराजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have gathered eleven akshauhinis, king; the enemy have only seven. How could I be defeated?"}},{"n":63,"text":"बलं त्रिगुणतो हीनं योध्यं प्राह बृहस्पतिः ।\nपरेभ्यस्त्रिगुणा चेयं मम राजन्ननीकिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brihaspati said that an army inferior by a third may be fought; my army is three times the enemy's, king."}},{"n":64,"text":"गुणहीनं परेषां च बहु पश्यामि भारत ।\nगुणोदयं बहुगुणमात्मनश्च विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see much lacking in the enemy's qualities, and in mine much excellence of many qualities."}},{"n":65,"text":"एतत्सर्वं समाज्ञाय बलाग्र्यं मम भारत ।\nन्यूनतां पाण्डवानां च न मोहं गन्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding all this, my superior strength and the Pandavas' smallness, you should not be bewildered."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":66,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा संजयं भूयः पर्यपृच्छत भारत ।\nविधित्सुः प्राप्तकालानि ज्ञात्वा परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Bharata, he asked Sanjaya again, wishing to act, knowing the times at hand, that conqueror of enemy cities."}}]}]}